@startuml formatting-sequence
title Formatting (A9) -- manual Reformat Code vs. Format on Save

participant "ide-ui\n(IdeApp)" as UI
participant "ide-lsp\n(LspClient)" as LSP
participant "rust-analyzer" as Server

== Manual Reformat Code (Cmd+Alt+L) ==
UI -> UI : trigger_reformat_code()\n(tab_size/insert_spaces from IndentUnit)
UI -> LSP : LspRequest::Format { path, tab_size, insert_spaces }

alt documentFormattingProvider not negotiated
  LSP --> UI : LspEvent::FormatReady { path, edit: None }\n(no wire traffic)
else negotiated
  LSP -> Server : textDocument/formatting
  Server --> LSP : TextEdit[] | null
  LSP -> LSP : wrap into a single-FileEdit WorkspaceEdit,\nor None if null/empty
  LSP --> UI : LspEvent::FormatReady { path, edit }
end

UI -> UI : handle_format_ready()\nBuffer::apply (one more undo step, dirty, not auto-saved)

== Format on Save ==
UI -> UI : try_save_active() -- synchronous save,\ncompletely unchanged, runs to completion first
note right of UI
  Save is never delayed by LSP.
  Only after it succeeds does the
  follow-up formatting request fire.
end note
UI -> UI : format_on_save_target = Some(path)
UI -> LSP : LspRequest::Format { path, tab_size, insert_spaces }
LSP -> Server : textDocument/formatting
Server --> LSP : TextEdit[] | null
LSP --> UI : LspEvent::FormatReady { path, edit }

UI -> UI : handle_format_ready()\nlocate tab by response's format_path -> idx
alt edit is Some and idx found
  UI -> UI : tabs[idx].buffer.apply(edit) -- buffer now formatted, dirty
  UI -> UI : format_on_save_target matches idx's path\n-> save_tab_at(idx) again, silently\n(by index -- never self.active_tab)
  note right of UI
    File on disk was briefly unformatted
    between the two saves -- accepted,
    see doc §3.4 for why blocking the
    first save was rejected instead.
    save_tab_at(idx) targets the tab that
    was actually reformatted, even if a
    different tab is active by now.
  end note
else edit is None, or tab closed meanwhile
  UI -> UI : nothing to reapply or resave
end
UI -> UI : format_on_save_target = None

@enduml
